users/Dengnifer/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Dengnifer/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "mipstarre-review pr=587 head=6d79bfcffb209e6ee30df907146671a0b719a95c\n<!-- mipstarre-review pr=587 head=6d79bfcffb209e6ee30df907146671a0b719a95c -->\n# Review - PR 587 @ 6d79bfcffb209e6ee30df907146671a0b719a95c\n\nIndependent review by a Claude Opus helper (owner-authorized 2026-09-17); no author, fixer or prior reviewer context reused. Trusted prompt, persona and policy ref: 0a2182d59af621ebbd6a36b03c79c77c48566d53. Four files, 474 insertions and 7 deletions against merge-base 66d359d6fd79e9322f183889390772aa7cfbc87c on base branch main: one new 314-line Lean module with eleven declarations (a finite root-count / POVM obstruction), one umbrella import, one preserved historical audit and a bounded paper-gap-note edit.\n\n## Findings\n\n- [ ] F1 (code; minor) MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/QuadraticPointObstruction.lean:17-18 - the module docstring's References block cites `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex`, subsection \"Unrestricted point witnesses in the extended-line assertion\", but no such heading exists at this head: the file's only relevant heading is `\\subsection{The extended-line supplied-point obstruction}` (docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex:215), and `git grep -i \"Unrestricted point witnesses\"` over `docs/` and `blueprint/` at this head returns nothing. The locator the module points readers at for its mathematical justification does not resolve. Fix: name the existing subsection (the quadratic material is at :255-320 inside it). The two paper locators and both blueprint labels in the same block are correct, so this is the only dangling reference.\n\n## Review\n\nReviewed the published head; the PR worktree HEAD is the same sha. Exact-head CI is green: `local-ci/summary` success with build, proof-debt, proof-evasion, statement-origin, blueprint-sync, blueprint-render, paper-gaps and file-length all success. No prior marked review exists on this PR, so no earlier finding needed resolution.\n\nDuplication against main (the main point of this preservation packet). I grepped `github/main` for each of the eleven added names - `card_affine_quadratic_agreement_le_two`, `randomized_affine_quadratic_agreement_le`, `quadraticJointMeasurement`, `exists_quadratic_point_witness`, `quadraticJointMeasurement_postprocess`, `affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge`, `affine_povm_completed_quadratic_defect_ge`, `deterministic_defect_nonneg`, `uniform_affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge`, `eightElementParams`, `eight_element_affine_povm_obstruction` - and for the namespace `QuadraticPointObstruction`: none occurs on main. The three generic duplicates are genuinely replaced by reuse, not re-declared: `deterministicMeasurement` and `deterministicMeasurement_projective` come from `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Completeness/HonestStrategy/MeasurementFamily.lean:41,47`, `deterministicMeasurement_effect_self` / `_eq_zero_of_ne` from `Commutation.lean:185` and `MeasurementFamily.lean:70`, and `Measurement.postprocess_comp` from `MIPStarRE/LDT/Basic/SubMeasurementFamilies.lean:213`. Every other cited helper exists on main at the name used (`CombinedPointsWitness.exists_error_of_projective`, `linePolynomialOfCoefficients*`, `evalCoefficient`, `consistencyDefect_eq_one_sub_overlap`, `consistency_term_eq_stateQForm`, `avgOver_*`, `stateQForm_*`). I checked the one new helper that looked replaceable, `deterministic_defect_nonneg`: main's nonnegativity facts (`Combining/Lines/ConsistencyPositivity.lean:122` and `Combining/WitnessErrorNonneg.lean`) are stated for `ProjectiveSetting`-placed measurements on opposite registers and do not cover a bare `M : X -> Measurement A iota` on `EuclideanSpace`, so it is not a duplicate and its docstring says exactly why it needs no commutation hypothesis.\n\nMathematics and faithfulness. `card_affine_quadratic_agreement_le_two` is the honest root count: `f - C alpha * X^2` is nonzero because its degree-2 coefficient is `-alpha`, has natDegree at most 2, and the agreement set injects into its roots. `randomized_affine_quadratic_agreement_le` averages that over POVM weights with the degree hypothesis correctly guarded by `w a != 0`, giving `2 / card K`. `affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge` then uses the repository's own `consistencyDefect` on an arbitrary unit state, with the degree hypothesis guarded by `M.effect a != 0` (weaker than assuming all answers affine), so the `1 - 2/q` lower bound is a real obstruction and not a vacuous or conclusion-shaped statement; the completed-alphabet variant reduces to it by an `Option` split with both `none` terms shown to vanish. `uniform_affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge` lets the measurement depend on `alpha` but not on `x`, which is the correct quantifier order for the counterexample, and splits `alpha = 0` off using nonnegativity rather than smuggling a nonzero-`alpha` hypothesis into the average: `(1 - 1/q)(1 - 2/q)`. At `eightElementParams` (q=8, m=1, d=1; `hdvd` is `1 | 8`, `hq` is `8 = 2^3`) that is `(7/8)(6/8) = 21/32`, matching the stated constant, with answers `Fin 2 -> PauliScalar` decoded by main's `evalCoefficient` and degree bounded by main's `linePolynomialOfCoefficients_natDegree_le`. None of these are paper-labelled: the docstrings say \"formalization-only counterexample calculations for issue #511, not claims from the paper\", and the paper locators they do give check out (`lem:qld-4-13` is at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1034`, `claim:17-1` at :1140-1173); both blueprint labels `lem:qld-4-13-established` and `rem:qld-4-13-source-defects` exist in `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex`. No `\\leanok` is added anywhere.\n\nProof integrity and scope. No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `native_decide` or unsafe option in the diff. `Combining/Apply.lean` and `Combining/PointErrorObstruction.lean` are byte-identical to main (empty diff), and Apply.lean still carries exactly its three open statements at :80, :115, :157 - the recorded open scope is honest. I re-ran `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/QuadraticPointObstruction.lean` in the PR worktree: exit 0 with no diagnostics. The umbrella edit is a single import placed before `Combining.Apply`. Commit subjects follow `type(scope): imperative` under 72 characters and contain no closing reference.\n\nProse. The gap-note edit is accurate against the Lean it cites: \"for nonzero alpha the defect is at least 1-2/q\", \"averaging alpha yields (1-1/q)(1-2/q)\", \"at (q,m,d)=(8,1,1) the scalar average is at least 21/32\" and \"the quadratic joint point family admits a finite-error witness on every projective setting\" correspond one-to-one to `affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge`, `uniform_affine_povm_quadratic_defect_ge`, `eight_element_affine_povm_obstruction` and `exists_quadratic_point_witness`. The 21/256 figure is explicitly qualified as not transported to the directly indexed line-point law (footnote, and again in the audit), consistent with the pre-existing 1/8 X-axis-mass paragraph at :255-280 and with the fact that this PR proves only the scalar average; that qualification is the load-bearing sentence and it is present in both places. The deleted clause \"the formal perfect-strategy construction ... remain to be supplied\" is correctly dropped: `exists_spcc_value_one` (MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Completeness.lean:266) is proved and that file has no `sorry` at this head, so the replacement footnote sentence is true. The archived audit carries a valid YAML header with `status: historical`, and its 2026-09-18 status block cites base `364cc2e1`, which I verified is an ancestor of this head. Its historical body still says the perfect-strategy construction \"is also still admitted\", which is stale as of this head; the status block disclaims the body as the September 12 record, so I do not raise it as a finding, but the main session may prefer one more clause in that block naming `exists_spcc_value_one` alongside the two witness theorems it already updates.\n\nNot checked: I ran no full build (CI's build step is green at this head) and did not re-derive axiom closures with `#print axioms` (the PR body reports `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`; the module is `sorry`-free by grep and elaborates cleanly). I did not review PR 547's own history, which is out of scope by instruction, nor the unchanged `PointErrorObstruction.lean` internals.\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=APPROVED)\n", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/587#pullrequestreview-5243849416", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/587", "author_association": "OWNER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/587#pullrequestreview-5243849416"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/587"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-09-18T03:04:37Z", "commit_id": "6d79bfcffb209e6ee30df907146671a0b719a95c"}, "pr580": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pulls/580", "id": 4562252814, "node_id": "PR_kwDOUJyJf88AAAABD-50Dg", "html_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/580", "diff_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/580.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/pull/580.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/580", "number": 580, "state": "open", "locked": false, "title": "feat(QPBT/Extraction): preserve nonencoding mass bound", "user": {"login": "Dengnif